00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.300
Agents. Everybody's talking about them,
but nobody really seems to agree on what

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.940
they actually are. In Sim, the answer is
pretty simple. An agent is just a workflow

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.880
that can reason through agent blocks. That
means everything you already know about

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:20.540
building workflows still applies. You're
just giving them the ability to think for

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:25.220
themselves. And once that clicks, you'll
see how workflows can be more than basic

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:30.020
automations and power AI systems that
genuinely think and adapt. Let me show you

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.680
what I mean. Here's a workflow that runs
the same way every time. It scores a lead,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:41.600
then writes the result to a table.
Deterministic and predictable. Swap the

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.400
scoring step for an agent block, and that
one step starts to think, reasoning about

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.760
each lead instead of following a fixed
rule. An agent block is where it thinks.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.560
Running it spins up a fresh chat, like
ChatGPT or Claude, but driven by your

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.340
workflow. And it works in a loop, calling
tools, reading what comes back, and

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.980
changing course when it has to. The
homepage had no pricing, so it just opened

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.140
the pricing page itself.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.360
Compose blocks around it, and a
deterministic pipeline becomes an

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.020
intelligent one. And each agentic workflow
you build becomes a block for the next.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:21.480
And these systems only get more capable
over time. As the models improve, the same

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.760
workflows improve with them.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:29.120
Sim keeps up to date with the latest
models, patterns, and AI techniques, so

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.780
the newest capabilities are always
available. As you get more familiar with

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.480
Sim, you'll see how serious agentic
systems are assembled from the same simple

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.560
blocks and workflows.
